WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.222
"The Third Way to Boost NAD+"

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.360
There are three
NAD+ boosting strategies:

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.200
Increasing the supply
of NAD+ precursors

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.480
is just one way.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.040
The other two
are having the body make more,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.520
by activating
NAD+-synthesizing enzymes,

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.120
or have the body use less,
by, for example,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.600
conserving it, by using less.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.040
Besides sirtuins,
the major consumers

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.800
of NAD+ are PARP-1 and CD38.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.920
PARP-1 is an enzyme
that uses NAD+ to repair DNA.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.960
The more oxidative DNA damage,

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.360
the more single
and double stranded DNA breaks,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.040
the more enzymes like PARP-1
need to be activated

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.920
to come to the rescue.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.200
This uses up a lot of NAD.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.400
As DNA damage
accumulates with age,

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.000
the rising need
for repair enzymes like PARP-1

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.720
causes a major drain
on NAD+ levels.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.760
Exposing cells in vitro
to DNA damaging agents,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.000
such as gamma radiation
or genotoxic chemicals,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.320
can cause an 80
to 90 percent drop

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.400
in NAD+ levels
within a matter of minutes.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.720
This has led to the search
for PARP-1 blockers

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.960
to preserve NAD+ levels,

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.840
but rather than blocking
DNA repair,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.000
why not work to prevent
so much damage

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.520
in the first place?

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.400
For example,
the severe oxidative stress

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.040
of a high-fat diet

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.080
can lead to PARP-1 activation
and NAD+ depletion in mice,

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.920
but NAD+ levels can be
"dramatically restored"

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.760
by feeding them
"purple sweet potato color,"

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.840
the natural
anthocyanin pigments

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.200
found in purple sweet potatoes.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.840
Or, of course, you can just not
feed them a high-fat diet.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.920
DNA repair is a good thing.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.360
PARP-1 may be
one of the reasons

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.160
NAD+-boosting interventions
can improve healthspans

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.600
and lifespans
in laboratory animals.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.160
Greater PARP activity
strongly correlates

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.760
with longer lifespan

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.880
across about a dozen
mammalian species,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.120
and the PARP activity
of human centenarians

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.880
averages 60 percent higher
than younger controls.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.960
However, persistent activation
can lead to NAD+ depletion,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.600
and overactivation
can lead to cell death.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.280
So, we should try to keep
oxidative stress to a minimum.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.080
CD38 is another major guzzler
of NAD+.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.880
It's an enzyme that uses NAD+

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.920
found concentrated
on the surfaces

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.320
of immune cells
and robustly induced

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.600
in the context of inflammation.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.280
The rise of CD38 activity
with age

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:37.720
has been blamed on persistent
"inflammaging" activation,

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.560
the rise in systemic low-grade
inflammation in our bodies

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.600
when we get older,

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.360
which may be a major culprit
for falling NAD+ levels.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.880
For example, blocking CD38
has been found

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.280
to raise NAD+ levels
in old mice

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.600
comparable to that
of younger mice.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.680
So, oxidation and inflammation

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.160
can lead to a drop
in NAD+ levels,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.920
due to the excess activation
of the NAD+ consuming enzymes.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.480
This may explain why
protective sirtuin activity

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.480
is reduced in obesity,
a condition characterized

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.160
by oxidative stress
and inflammation.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.440
A study of identical twin pairs

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.040
in which one, on average,
was obese and the other not,

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.920
found significantly
less sirtuin expression

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.560
in the obese twin,

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.960
despite having
the same genetics.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.000
And randomize people
to a six-month trial

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.400
of 25 percent
calorie restriction,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.600
and you can show a boost
in sirtuin expression

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:36.200
along with a decrease
in DNA damage.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.320
Protein restriction
may have a similar effect,

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.360
since men and women
with higher protein intake

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.440
tend to have lower levels
of NAD+ in their blood,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.440
thought to be due
to the oxidative stress

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:49.280
induced by protein
breakdown byproducts.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.760
If oxidation and inflammation
are responsible

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.640
for a drop in NAD+ levels,

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.600
then what about the antioxidant

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.840
and anti-inflammatory
phytonutrients

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.760
in healthy plant foods?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.680
After screening
more than 14,000 compounds,

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.400
almost all flavonoids
were found to be effective

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.920
in a test for CD38 inhibition.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.720
The two most effective
were cyanidin,

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.200
found in red cabbage
and blackberries,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.560
and quercetagetin,
found in marigold flower tea.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.920
Another study found
the three most potent compounds

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.000
were luteolin, kuromanin,
and luteolinidin.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:28.240
Luteolin is found concentrated
in oregano, radicchio,

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.720
and chrysanthemum tea.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.720
Kuromanin is found
in black berries, purple corn,

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.320
and hibiscus tea.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.840
Corn tortillas are
surprisingly easy to make;

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.560
so why not choose blue
or purple masa

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.520
to make them even healthier?

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.320
Luteolinidin,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.040
found to increase NAD+
in the hearts of rats,

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.280
can be found in red sorghum,

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.960
one of the components
of my prebiotic BROL mix,

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.840
when I can find it.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:54.280
The flavonoid apigenin

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:57.120
is a well-established
CD38 inhibitor.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.680
When given to mice,
apigenin boosts NAD+ levels

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.720
by about 50 percent,
which is what people would get

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:07.640
taking the maximum
tolerable daily dose of NR.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:12.160
The best sources are parsley
and chamomile tea.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.040
A wide range of flavonoids
found in green tea, turmeric,

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.960
and fruits and vegetables
have also been found

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.360
to prevent NAD+ depletion
in human cells in vitro

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.200
at levels found in the blood
after consumption.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.240
How much do you have to eat,
though?

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.240
Proanthocyanidins have been
found to lower PARP-1

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:32.520
and CD38 expression in rats.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.440
NAD+ and sirtuin activity
was significantly boosted

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.920
at the human equivalent dose
of about 280 milligrams a day.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.640
How much is that?

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.640
That's the amount
of proanthocyanidins

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.880
found in a single apple.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.400
You could also reach that dose
eating two plums,

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.320
a half cup of wild blueberries,

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.520
a little over a teaspoon
of cinnamon,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.160
or a little over a tablespoon,
like four teaspoons,

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.480
of cocoa powder.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.400
Quercetin is another suppressor
of PARP-1 and CD38

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.440
shown to increase
sirtuin activity in mice.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.480
The concentration necessary
to lower PARP-1 in vitro

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:10.560
can be achieved by taking
a quercetin supplement,

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.520
but typical supplement
manufacturers'

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.200
recommended doses
are up to 100 times

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.520
the average daily
dietary intake.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.600
Thankfully, food works too.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.040
Researchers fried up
one and a half yellow onions

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.640
and raised
quercetin blood levels

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:27.000
to about 75 percent there.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.640
And so, two onions might do it.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.560
There's no long-term
safety data

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.680
on high-dose
flavonoid supplementation;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:36.000
so, public health researchers
suggest

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.880
"caution should be exercised
in ingesting them

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.360
at levels above which
would be obtained

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:59.400
from a typical
vegetarian diet."

